:R-HSA-1980143  a           owl:NamedIndividual , obo:GO_0007219 ;
        rdfs:comment        "NOTCH1 functions as both a transmembrane receptor presented on the cell surface and as a transcriptional regulator in the nucleus.<br><br>NOTCH1 receptor presented on the plasma membrane is activated by a membrane bound ligand expressed in trans on the surface of a neighboring cell. In trans, ligand binding triggers proteolytic cleavage of NOTCH1 and results in release of the NOTCH1 intracellular domain, NICD1, into the cytosol.<br><br>NICD1 translocates to the nucleus where it associates with RBPJ (also known as CSL or CBF) and mastermind-like (MAML) proteins (MAML1, MAML2 or MAML3; possibly also MAMLD1) to form NOTCH1 coactivator complex. NOTCH1 coactivator complex activates transcription of genes that possess RBPJ binding sites in their promoters. <br><br>" ;
        rdfs:label          "Signaling by NOTCH1" ;
        dc:contributor      "Edited: Orlic-Milacic, M, 2012-02-10" , "Edited: D'Eustachio, P, 2012-02-06" , "Authored: Egan, SE, Orlic-Milacic, M, 2011-11-14" , "Reviewed: Haw, R, 2012-02-06" , "GOC:reactome_curators" ;
        dc:date             "2023-06-21" ;
        pav:providedBy      "https://reactome.org" ;
        oboInOwl:hasDbXref  "R-HSA-1980143" ;
        skos:narrower       <http://model.geneontology.org/R-HSA-157118/R-HSA-157118> ;
        skos:note           "org.biopax.paxtools.model.level3.Pathway" .

